==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|inseminatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|inseminare||to sow}}. See {{m|en|seminate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈsɛmɪneɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-inseminate.oga|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[sow]] (to disperse or plant seeds).
# To fill with one's [[semen]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} To [[impregnate]] (to cause to become pregnant).

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|insemination}}
* {{l|en|inseminator}}

